Package: rasch
Type: Package
Title: Models and Diagnostics for Rasch Measurement Theory
Version: 1.14.2
Authors@R: person("Josh", "McGrane", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "drjoshmcgrane@gmail.com")
Description: Fits the models of Rasch Measurement Theory (Rasch, 1960
    <ISBN:9780226705538>; 1961 <https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.bsmsp/1200512895>):
    the dichotomous Rasch model, the polytomous Rasch models, many-facet
    Rasch models, the extended frame of reference model, and comparative
    judgement models for dichotomous and polytomous pairwise comparisons.
    Estimation is by pairwise conditional maximum likelihood (Zwinderman,
    1995 <doi:10.1177/014662169501900406>) with person measures by weighted
    likelihood (Warm, 1989 <doi:10.1007/BF02294627>); anchored estimation
    and planned missing-data designs are supported. Diagnostics include
    tests of fit, targeting, dimensionality, local response dependence,
    differential item functioning, threshold functioning, reliability, and
    equating, following Andrich and Marais (2019)
    <doi:10.1007/978-981-13-7496-8>. Also provides simulation tools and an
    interactive 'shiny' interface.
URL: https://drjoshmcgrane.github.io/rasch/, https://github.com/drjoshmcgrane/rasch
BugReports: https://github.com/drjoshmcgrane/rasch/issues
